      "runbook_title": "Recovery Procedures Runbook",
      "runbook_text": "=== DISASTER RECOVERY RUNBOOK ===\n\n1. DATABASE RECOVERY\n   a. Stop all application services\n   b. Locate latest verified backup from Backup Verification tab\n   c. Copy backup file to data/ directory\n   d. Rename to university.db (or configured DB name)\n   e. Run integrity check: PRAGMA integrity_check;\n   f. Restart application services\n   g. Verify data consistency\n\n2. CONFIGURATION RECOVERY\n   a. Restore config files from data/config/ backup\n   b. Verify email_config.json, api_server_config.json\n   c. Check backup configuration in data_backup/config.py\n   d. Restart affected services\n\n3. FULL SYSTEM RESTORE\n   a. Restore database (Step 1)\n   b. Restore configuration (Step 2)\n   c. Restore uploaded files from data/uploads/ backup\n   d. Restore log files if needed\n   e. Clear any temp files in data/temp/\n   f. Run full system health check\n   g. Verify all integrations (API, Email, Backup)\n\n4. FAILOVER PROCEDURE\n   a. Notify all administrators via configured webhooks\n   b. Switch to backup server if available\n   c. Update DNS/load balancer if applicable\n   d. Monitor system metrics for 24 hours\n   e. Document incident in activity log\n\n5. POST-RECOVERY CHECKLIST\n   [ ] Database integrity verified\n   [ ] All API endpoints responding\n   [ ] Email service operational\n   [ ] Backup scheduler re-enabled\n   [ ] Activity log recording events\n   [ ] User sessions validated\n   [ ] Admin notification sent",
